.TH PAM_PIV_KEYRING 8 "2026-10-02" "piv-keyring" "Linux-PAM Manual"
.SH NAME
pam_piv_keyring \- unlock the GNOME login keyring after smartcard, FIDO2 or password login
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pam_piv_keyring.so
.RB [ mode=piv | mode=login ]
.RB [ file=\fIpath\fR ]
.RB [ module=\fIpkcs11.so\fR ]
.RB [ only_if=\fIservice\fR,... ]
.RB [ prompt_pin ]
.RB [ nofido2 ]
.RB [ debug ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The login keyring is protected by a random 256-bit secret.  The secret is stored
in a per-user wrap file, sealed separately for each enrolled unlock method
("slot"): a PIV card key, a FIDO2 security key (hmac-secret extension) or the
login password (Argon2id).  Enrol with
.BR piv-keyring (1).
.PP
In the auth stack the module recovers the secret and sets it as PAM_AUTHTOK, so
.B pam_gnome_keyring
(which must come after it) unlocks the keyring with it.
.PP
In the password stack it re-wraps the password slot when the login password is
changed, using PAM_OLDAUTHTOK and PAM_AUTHTOK as set by
.BR pam_unix (8).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B mode=piv
PAM_AUTHTOK holds the card PIN, as forwarded by
.B pam_sss forward_pass
after smartcard authentication.  The module logs in to the card with it and
unwraps the secret.  If that fails, PAM_AUTHTOK is cleared so that the PIN is
never used as a keyring password.  The PIN is never tried when the token reports
it locked or on its final try, or when its length is outside the token's range.
Only place this mode where PAM_AUTHTOK can only be a PIN.
.TP
.B mode=login
(default) If PAM_AUTHTOK is set, it is the login password and unlocks the
password slot.  If it is not set (for example after passwordless
.BR pam_u2f (8)),
the module asks for a touch on an enrolled FIDO2 security key.
.TP
.BI file= path
Wrap file; %h is the home directory, %u the user name.
Default: %h/.local/share/piv-keyring/login.wrap.  The file is read with the
user's filesystem credentials and must be owned by the user and not group or
world writable.
.TP
.BI module= path
PKCS#11 module used to reach the card (default: OpenSC).
.TP
.BI only_if= services
Only act for these comma-separated PAM services.
.TP
.B prompt_pin
mode=piv: ask for the PIN if PAM_AUTHTOK is empty.
.TP
.B nofido2
mode=login: never ask for a security key touch.
.TP
.B debug
Log more.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pam.d/gdm-smartcard-sssd-piv-keyring
GDM smartcard stack using mode=piv, installed as an alternative for
/etc/pam.d/gdm-smartcard.
.TP
.I /usr/share/pam-configs/piv-keyring
pam-auth-update profile adding mode=login (for gdm-password) and the password
stack hook.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR piv-keyring (1),
.BR pam_gnome_keyring (8),
.BR pam_sss (8),
.BR pam_u2f (8)
